# Rules — Konter Print Helper

## Proyek

- Repo: Flutter mobile (`pubspec` name `cetak_struk`), app title **Daru Cell**.
- Fitur inti: OCR struk + cetak thermal Bluetooth.
- Path lokal tipikal: `/home/ndaruls/Projects/MOBILE/konter-print-helper`.
- Artefak bot (audit/report/plan/log): `/home/ndaruls/Workspace/konter-print-helper-history/` — jangan campur subjek atau tulis ke root Workspace.

## Persona & bahasa

- Jawab ringkas, jelas, bahasa Indonesia kecuali user minta lain.
- Fokus aksi: perbaikan, implementasi, penjelasan singkat yang bisa dijalankan.
- Jangan mengarang path, versi, atau hasil perintah yang belum dijalankan.

## Design system

- UI mengikuti `Docs/design-system.md` dan `.cursor/rules/design-system.mdc`.
- Primary: `#8F00BF` / `Color(0xFF8F00BF)`.
- Jangan pakai branding indigo sistem-sekolah di app ini.

## Kode Flutter / Dart

- Prefer `Theme.of(context)` / `ColorScheme` daripada warna hardcode.
- Widget kecil, stateful hanya bila perlu; pisahkan logic (services/providers) dari UI.
- Handle permission Bluetooth/kamera dengan pesan error yang bisa dipahami kasir.
- Jangan commit secret, keystore password, atau file `.env` berisi kredensial.

## Git

- Jangan `git push` / force-push / amend pushed commit tanpa perintah eksplisit user.
- Commit hanya jika diminta; pesan commit singkat dan deskriptif.

## Graphify Tool — MANDATORY

This project has a graphify knowledge graph at `graphify-out/`.

Always-on rule also lives in `.cursor/rules/graphify.mdc` (from `graphify install --platform cursor`).

**MANDATORY: Before using Read, Grep, Glob, or Bash to explore the codebase, you MUST run graphify first:**

- `graphify query "<question>"` — scoped subgraph for any codebase or architecture question
- `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` — dependency path between two symbols
- `graphify explain "<concept>"` — all nodes related to a concept

This applies to YOU and to every subagent you spawn. Include this rule explicitly in every subagent prompt that involves code exploration. Do not skip graphify because files are "already known" or because you are executing a plan — the graph surfaces cross-file dependencies and INFERRED edges that grep and Read cannot find.

Only use Read/Grep/Glob directly when:

1. graphify has already oriented you and you need to modify or debug specific lines
2. `graphify-out/graph.json` does not exist yet

- If `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` exists, navigate it instead of reading raw files
- Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` only for broad architecture review when query/path/explain do not surface enough context
- After modifying code files, run `graphify update .` to keep the graph current (AST-only, no API cost)

